From a12a189e7f08d39c89092a8410395cbe2d26f53a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shine5402 <14089306+shine5402@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:55:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] QQuickPopupWindow: close the whole menu chain on a press on
 the menu bar

When a Popup.Window menu opened from a MenuBar is open, a press on the
menu bar is meant to close every open menu and be swallowed, so that the
MenuBar doesn't reopen the menu right away. Since CloseMultiple, that
branch closes them through closePopups(), which keeps a popup open while
a CloseOnPressOutsideParent press lands inside its parent item.
QQuickMenuBarItem gives its menu exactly that policy, with itself as the
parent item. Pressing the title of an open menu therefore closed nothing
but its submenus, and swallowed the press: the menu stayed open, and
the title could not close it. Qt 6.10 closed the whole chain here.

Close every menu from the popup up through its transient-parent popup
windows unconditionally, as the comment there already says.
